# Synth — AI-Driven UI Testing Tool

## Project Overview

Synth is a CLI tool where UI tests are written in plain English (markdown) and an AI agent drives a real browser via Playwright to verify them.

## Tech Stack

- TypeScript (ESM, ES2022, NodeNext modules)
- Playwright (browser automation)
- Vercel AI SDK (`ai` package) for multi-provider LLM support
- Commander.js (CLI), Zod (validation), tsup (build), Vitest (tests)

## Architecture

```
Tests (.test.md) → Parser → Agent Loop:
  Capture page state (screenshot + ARIA tree)
  → Send to AI (generateText + tool_use)
  → AI returns action (click, type, navigate, assert, done)
  → Execute via Playwright
  → Repeat until done(pass/fail)
```

## Key Patterns

- Tools defined with `tool()` from Vercel AI SDK using Zod schemas (`src/ai/tools.ts`)
- Agent loop uses `generateText()` with `maxSteps` for multi-step tool calling (`src/agent/loop.ts`)
- Multi-strategy selector resolution: CSS → text → role → label → placeholder → testId (`src/browser/actions.ts`)
- The `done` tool has no execute function — checked in the agent loop's step results
- Fresh browser page per test for isolation
- Config validated with Zod, loaded from `synth.config.ts` with CLI overrides

## File Conventions

- Source code in `src/`, tests in `tests/unit/` and `tests/integration/`
- Test files use `.test.ts` extension
- Imports use `.js` extension (NodeNext module resolution)
- Templates for `synth init` are in `templates/`

## Commands

- `npm run dev -- run tests/` — run in dev mode
- `npm run build` — build with tsup
- `npm test` — vitest
- `npm run lint` — tsc --noEmit
